    "title": "Indiana Fever Lose to New York Liberty Before All-Star Break",
    "text": "• The Indiana Fever lost to the New York Liberty 98-77 on July 16, 2025.\n• Caitlin Clark was sidelined with a groin injury and ruled out just before tip-off.\n• This marked Clark's third absence of the season due to injury.\n• Breanna Stewart led the Liberty with 24 points, 11 rebounds, and seven assists.\n• Sabrina Ionescu contributed 15 points and nine assists for the Liberty.\n• Fever head coach Stephanie White emphasized the need for consistency and a 'reset' heading into the All-Star break.\n• Clark is scheduled to compete in the 3-point contest and was named a captain for the All-Star Game.\n• White stated that there has been no discussion about Clark's availability for the All-Star weekend.\n• Clark is dealing with her second groin injury of the year, which occurred in the final minutes of a previous game.\n• The Fever's record without Clark is now 4-6.\n• Kelsey Mitchell led the Fever in scoring with 16 points.\n• The Fever will face the Liberty again on Tuesday after the All-Star break.",
